摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"极简·省 token 的 DSH 长期记忆插件：零 LLM 自动捕获、符号索引渐进披露、ESR 证据闭环。Minimalist token-saving memory for DeepSeek Harness: zero-LLM auto-capture, symbolic index, ESR-lite evidence closure.","id":"gh:1338237286","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-engram","slug":"skepsun/dsh-engram","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","long-term-memory","memory","pi-esr"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"极简·省 token 的 DSH 长期记忆插件：零 LLM 自动捕获、符号索引渐进披露、ESR 证据闭环。Minimalist token-saving memory for DeepSeek Har"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ness: zero-LLM auto-capture, symbolic index, ESR-lite evidence closure."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-engram"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> **English · 中文**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Minimalist long-term memory for DeepSeek Harness, distilled from the\nsymbolic-index and pi-esr ideas"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" —\nwith one goal: **save tokens**."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- **Zero-LLM intake** — auto-captures meaningful events from tool results by pure\npattern matching ("},{"id":"p5s2","text":"git milestones with a written `-m` commit message, edits to\nkey files, repeated errors), plus an exp"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"licit `engram_store`. Nothing on the hot\npath calls a model, and pure plumbing — `git push` / `git s"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"tash` / silent\ncommits — is deliberately never recorded (see *Auto-capture policy* below).\nEvery wri"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"te is run through a deterministic **secret redactor** first — API\nkeys, JWTs, `Bearer` tokens, priva"},{"id":"p5s6","text":"te keys, AWS/Stripe/Slack/GitHub tokens and\n`key=value` secret shapes are replaced with `<REDACTED:…"},{"id":"p5s7","text":">` markers before the\ndedup hash, the char cap, and storage, so sensitive text can never land on\ndis"},{"id":"p5s8","text":"k. Failing **test runs** are recognized by pure patterns (`npm test`,\n`node --test`, vitest/pytest/j"},{"id":"p5s9","text":"est, failure lines) and captured as\n`tags:[\"error\",\"test\"]` entries with a raised signal. DSH **goal"},{"id":"p5s10","text":"-domain\nintegration**: a completed or blocked goal (`goal/change` session event)\nauto-sediments as a"},{"id":"p5s11","text":" `handoff`/`error` memory (`tag:goal`), so the outcome of\na goal survives its session (see the `GET "},{"id":"p5s12","text":"/api/dsh-engram/goals` read surface).\n- **User-correction / preference learning (`autoCapturePrefere"},{"id":"p5s13","text":"nces`, default on,\nzero LLM)** — the lesson that \"when the AI makes a mistake and gets corrected,\nth"},{"id":"p5s14","text":"at lesson should persist\" (correx,\nPAHF, Mem0 preference extraction): a\n`session/event` listener wat"},{"id":"p5s15","text":"ches `user/message` and turns deterministic\ncorrection/preference cues into a dedicated `preference`"},{"id":"p5s16","text":" memory kind —\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Why another memory plugin?"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Surveys of the existing DSH plugin ecosystem show the recall-bridge, approval-gate,\nLLM-distillation"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" and vector/graph niches are already crowded. dsh-engram fills the\nthree gaps that matter for token "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"/graph niches are already crowded. dsh-engram fills the\nthree gaps that matter for token discipline:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"1. **No model in the write path** — capture is deterministic pattern matching.\n2. **No raw text in t"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"he prompt** — a bounded symbolic index is injected, plus the\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Security model"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"The DSH plugin ecosystem is young and unvetted — there is no official directory,\nno signature check,"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" and the harness's read/write permission tiers do **not**\nconstrain what a plugin's own code can do."},{"id":"p10s3","text":" So the trust bar for a memory plugin\nis higher than for a tool: a memory plugin sits on your prompt"},{"id":"p10s4","text":" prefix and writes\nto disk on your behalf. dsh-engram's model, stated plainly:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- **No network, ever.** The plugin has no outbound socket, no telemetry, no\nupdate pinger. Nothing h"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ere can leak your sessions off the machine.\n- **No shell, no filesystem access beyond one storage fi"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"le.** It never executes\ncommands and never touches arbitrary paths. All data lives in the single\nsto"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"rage-domain unit `~/.dsh/storages/dsh_engram.json` (plus the session-log\nreads it makes through DSH'"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"s own `ctx.sessionQuery`).\n- **Secrets are redacted before they can land on disk.** Every write path"},{"id":"p11s6","text":" —\n`engram_store`, auto-capture, and the import/restore route — runs text through\nthe deterministic "},{"id":"p11s7","text":"`redactText` rule engine (API keys, JWTs, `Bearer` tokens,\nprivate keys, `key=value` secret shapes) "},{"id":"p11s8","text":"*before* the dedup hash, the char\ncap, and storage. Nothing sensitive is ever persisted, so nothing "},{"id":"p11s9","text":"sensitive\ncan be recalled later.\n- **Doing harm requires your harness's own permissions.** The plugi"},{"id":"p11s10","text":"n only *asks*\nthe host to do things via the same seams the tools you already trust use. It\ndoes not "},{"id":"p11s11","text":"widen sandbox policy or escalate to `danger-full-access` — if you\nkeep your profile's defaults, engr"},{"id":"p11s12","text":"am inherits exactly those bounds.\n- **Read-mostly web API, loopback-fenced.** The GUI routes under\n`"},{"id":"p11s13","text":"/api/dsh-engram` reject any non-loopback caller unless you explicitly\nwhitelist a hostname via `trus"},{"id":"p11s14","text":"tedHosts`; even then the same-origin fence holds.\n- **Verifiable.** `npm run dsh-engram -- doctor` ("},{"id":"p11s15","text":"`/scripts/dsh-engram.mjs\ndoctor`) reports what the plugin is configured to touch; the whole store is"},{"id":"p11s16","text":"\ninspectable, nothing is opaque. If you ever doubt a claim in this section, the\ncode to check is `li"},{"id":"p11s17","text":"b/redact.js`, `lib/store.js` and this plugin's\n`cordis.patch.yml`."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"What this deliberately does **not** claim: it is not an air-gap. If your profile\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- **DSH 版本 / DSH versions**: `>=0.1.2-alpha.2 <0.3.0-0` (本版 `0.9.0`; 已发布的 `0.3.7`、`0.4.0` 仍声明旧的 `0.1"},{"id":"p14s2","text":".x` 范围 `>=0.1.2-alpha.2 <0.2.0-0` — 见下方矩阵)\n- **最后验证日期 / Last verified**: 2026-10-27 — DSH `0.2.1-rc."},{"id":"p14s3","text":"2` (`dsh --version`), web profile live composition; npm test 483/483\n- **安装方式已验证 / Verified install*"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"*: `dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-engram`"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"> **Short version.** Every **published** release (`0.2.0` … `0.3.6`) supports\n> the **old** DSH API "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"graph (`0.1.0-rc.7` / `0.1.1`, peers `^0.1.0-rc.7`)\n> **only**. DSH `0.1.2-alpha.2` and newer are **"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"not** compatible with those\n> releases — the settings/client API family broke there. New-DSH support"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"\n> **starts with `0.3.7`**, the first release of the new API generation\n> (described below)."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| dsh-engram release | Status | DSH support | Declared via |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| `0.2.0` … `0.3.6` (npm, GitHub v0.3.3–v0.3.6) | published | **old DSH only** — `0.1.0-rc.7` / `0.1"},{"id":"p17s2","text":".0-rc.8` / `0.1.1-rc.1` / `0.1.1-rc.2` | peers `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*@^0.1.0-rc.7` |\n| `0.3.7` / `0.4.0"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"` (npm) | published | **new DSH, settings `installSection`** — `>=0.1.2-alpha.2 <0.2.0-0` | `engines"},{"id":"p17s4","text":".dsh` + peers `>=0.1.2-alpha.2 <0.2.0-0` |\n| `0.5.0` (npm) | published | **DSH `0.1.2-alpha.2` … `<0"},{"id":"p17s5","text":".3.0-0`** — 设置卡迁移到 entry-id volatile Config（`0.1.7+`/`0.2.x`），`≤0.1.5` 自动回退 `installSection` | `engi"},{"id":"p17s6","text":"nes.dsh` + peers `>=0.1.2-alpha.2 <0.3.0-0` |\n| `0.5.1` | published | 同 `0.5.0` — 会话扫描修复（`session.v<"},{"id":"p17s7","text":"N>.jsonl.zstd`，issue #8）、数据导出/导入 GUI、替换/冲突可视化（issue #3） | 同 `0.5.0` |\n| `0.6.0` | published | 同 `0.5"},{"id":"p17s8","text":".0` — Context Ledger、BoundaryPrune/ResultPack 默认开 + 账本否决、JIT 推送、Context GC 改 opt-in | 同 `0.5.0` |\n| "},{"id":"p17s9","text":"`0.7.0` | published | 同 `0.5.0` — session episode、resume brief、entity pages/cards、revalidatable anch"},{"id":"p17s10","text":"ors + layered TTL | 同 `0.5.0` |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
